<h2 class="bde-heading-506-117 bde-heading">
How Much Is Mike Conley’s Contract Worth?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-118 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-141 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-154 bde-f-text">
<p>Conley signed with Boston as a free agent on July 6, 2026, a one-year veteran minimum contract worth <strong>$3.88m</strong> and fully guaranteed.</p>
<p>It’s the seventh contract of his career and the smallest since his rookie deal ended in 2011. The minimum is set by the league and scales with years of service. A 20-year veteran costs his club less than the figure suggests, because the league covers part of it.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-191 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="proportions">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/_ported/08ba6176394a.css">
<h3>Mike Conley’s Salary As a Percentage of Cap and Payroll</h3><div class="nf-proportion-layout"><div class="nf-proportions"><figure><div class="nf-donut" role="img" aria-label="2.35% of Salary Cap" style="--share:2.349966961888%"><span>2.35%<small class="nf-change nf-change-none" title="Previous-season comparison unavailable">—</small></span></div><figcaption>Salary Cap</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="nf-donut" role="img" aria-label="1.95% of Team Payroll" style="--share:1.9507256771036%"><span>1.95%<small class="nf-change nf-change-none" title="Previous-season comparison unavailable">—</small></span></div><figcaption>Team Payroll</figcaption></figure></div><div class="nf-proportion-copy"><p>Conley's <strong>$3.88m</strong> takes up <strong>2.35%</strong> of the <strong>$164.96m</strong> salary cap and <strong>1.95%</strong> of Boston's <strong>$198.72m</strong> payroll. The cap is a benchmark, and clubs are allowed to spend past it under certain rules.</p><p><a href="https://www.nba.com/news/free-agency-explained">How Do Salary Caps Work in the NBA?</a></p></div></div><script src="/_ported/8334868131c3.js" is:inline></script>
</div>
